      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that's the thing, the \"base-4\" logic is just the surface level. history is full of things later being proven to be more complex than the initial discovery. if the primes are the backbone of the encryption, then the nucleotide sequence is just the medium being used to carry it. i'm not saying it's a textbook fact yet, i'm saying the math feels inherently present in the coding. if you look at the way prime distributions guide complex systems, wouldn't it be a massive oversight to assume biological complexity wouldn't use that same logic for something much bigger than just \"heredity\"?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
